<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Brooke returns four weeks after his first visit. He has taken tamoxifen 20 mg every day for fifteen weeks and keeps the bottle by his toothbrush. He has mild hot flashes two or three times a week, mostly at night, which do not stop him sleeping. He has had no leg swelling or pain, chest pain, or breathlessness, and no change in vision. The mastectomy scars are comfortable and he has full movement of the right shoulder, with no arm swelling. He had his DXA scan this morning and saw Dr. Cho of medical oncology, who has taken over his tamoxifen and sent a germline genetic test today. He starts vitamin D today for the low level found at the first visit. He walks most days. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Tamoxifen</td><td>Fifteen weeks; no missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Side effects</td><td>Mild night hot flashes; no clot symptoms or visual change</td></tr><tr><td>Surgical sites</td><td>Comfortable; full right shoulder movement; no arm swelling</td></tr><tr><td>Coordination</td><td>Medical oncology seen today; germline test sent</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

